{"game": "space-marine-2011", "language": "english", "appid": 55150, "month": "2023-06", "window": 3, "start_date": 1686873600, "end_date": 1687478399, "month_true_total": 191, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-09 18:03:25 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "140494518", "author": {"steamid": "76561198010001199", "personaname": "Death and life?", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198010001199/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 97, "playtime_forever": 1011, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1011, "last_played": 1725873834, "avatar": "e0345d95a99a0280d31aaec05676eaad7a125d2c"}, "language": "english", "review": "I can't say this game is for everyone but for Warhammer fans its not bad just not overwhelmingly good. I did enjoy the combat system and the very somewhat mindless combat. A degree of tactics is needed just not many. I enjoyed playing the game on hard once and well that's it. I do not regret my purchase but for anyone else that is remotely interested I'd get it on sale and then play it once on hard. There is not much real story and that's really normal for warhammer games as any warhammer game should really only be about war and the fighting. If you want real warhammer story's or lore read one of their books or go onto youtube and listen to those, they are not bad.", "timestamp_created": 1687439172, "timestamp_updated": 1687439172, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1315281600", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "140474217", "author": {"steamid": "76561199229678974", "personaname": "BUDJJJJJJJJJ", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199229678974/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 17, "playti